-- title:
--   Common offset (round six, `tgt_slot`)
-- statement:
--   **Common offset.** In the target order, slot `(i, h)` with `b ≤ h < b + qK` sits in the
--   `i`-th chunk of chunk group `j = ⌊(qK-1-(h-b))/K⌋`, at offset `ρ = (h-b) mod K` from the least
--   significant end of that chunk (position `K-1-ρ` inside it).
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.SynthLayoutPaper`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem Synth.tgt_slot (hK : 0 < K) (i : Fin D) {h : ℕ} (hb : bb ℓ K ≤ h) (hh : h < bb ℓ K + qq ℓ K * K) :
--       let e := qq ℓ K * K - 1 - (h - bb ℓ K)
--       (tgtL D ℓ K long).getD ((lstL D ℓ K long).length + ((e / K) * D + i) * K + (e % K)) 0 =
--         nm D i h ∧ K - 1 - e % K = (h - bb ℓ K) % K
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** §6.2 Lemma 16: the paper's layout `L`
--
--   Axes `i < D` have `a_i = ℓ` (long) or `ℓ - 1` (short) address bits; slot `h` of axis `i` is named
--   `nm i h = h·D + i`. With `b = (ℓ-1) mod K` and `q = ⌊(ℓ-1)/K⌋`:
--
--   * the **prefix list** `Lst`: the top slots `(i, ℓ-1)` of the long axes (increasing `i`), then
--     `(i, h)` for `h = b-1, …, 0` and, within each `h`, increasing `i`;
--   * after the prefix moves every axis keeps the `qK` slots `h = ℓ-2, …, b` (`restA`), which are
--     `q` consecutive `K`-bit chunks (`chunk i j`, numbered from the top);
--   * the target order `tgt = Lst ++ (chunks in chunk-major order)`.
--
--   `paper_layout`: `L` is reached by `|Lst| ≤ D(b+1)` single moves and at most `Dq - 1` chunk
--   exchanges, and its array denotation is the `pull` by `relabel init tgt`.
--   `tgt_slot`: in the target, slot `(i, h)` (`b ≤ h ≤ ℓ-2`) lies in chunk `i` of chunk group
--   `j = ⌊(qK-1-(h-b))/K⌋`, at offset `(h - b) mod K` from the least significant end — the common
--   offset used by the simultaneous layer (Proposition 14).
--
